  "item": "lem-coef-simplicial-projective-model-calculus",
  "worker": "stage1",
  "summary": "No project attachment exists. All clauses retained. Constructed the enriched functor category via an accessible monad; supplied the two cellular lifting systems, retract recognition, simplicial pushout products, evaluation and Kan-extension formulas. Proved DK invariance through good relative units and an explicit fixed-object contractible-category factorization. Reused existing presentability, cellular, localization-detection, homotopy-representation and fixed-object simplicial-category nodes; no new nodes are necessary. Checked empty indexing categories, arbitrary generating domains and non-Kan mapping sets.",
  "blueprint": "Current main-20261015 prop-coef-integral-exceptional-adjoint.proof.md paragraph 2: coherent derived coefficient adjunction before its displayed RHom/Rlim calculation, via the item's existing enrichment/rectification ancestry. This is a generic model-theoretic tool and does not change the geometric unit route."
 },
 "reviewed": {
  "date": "2026-10-16",
  "by": "L",
  "reviewer": "NT-cc-NE-89555c471",
  "group": "NE",
  "result": "pass",
  "note": "mechanical checks by tools/merge_delivery.py; mathematics reviewed in full by NT-cc-NE-89555c471 (reviewer sub-agent of L); spot-checked: Read the item, all 13 steps and the full statements of all 12 cited nodes, which all sit in unit sk-prop-sf-biduality-general, so the route stays in the unit and there are no tool_uses. HTT is not archived locally, so I checked against my knowledge of HTT A.2.8.2 and A.3.3.2-A.3.3.8 rather than the text. The statement is the HTT projective case for Kan-model sSet with no hypothesis added or weakened (no left properness, cofibrant generating domains or local Kan condition). Steps 1-7: monad algebras are exactly the enriched functors; the free/evaluation and Kan-extension adjunctions are checked in each simplicial degree; the three smallness nodes' hypotheses hold; the pushout-product form of the simplicial model axiom is correctly derived from the cited node's mapping-space form; the retract argument gives the trivial cofibrations. Step 8: the unit at F_iX evaluated at k is v tensored with X, so the relative unit is s pushout-product I(i,k)->J(vi,vk), a trivial cofibration. Step 9: checked that pushouts and the Z_alpha transfinite sequence give relative units; H0=0 makes eta_P a trivial cofibration for cofibrant P. Step 10: Y^{Delta^1}->Y is a trivial fibration for fibrant Y, then detection and two-out-of-three in the naturality square. Step 11: derived unit invertible; derived restriction reflects isomorphisms via bifibrant representatives; counit by the triangle identity; not circular. Step 12: the factorization in sCat_O gives contractible D; the cofibration is injective on mapping sets (I->D->D' equals the injective free map); K=JxD; p, g, s are DK equivalences and g, s are injective on mapping sets. Step 13: s^*p^*=1 makes v^*=g^*p^* an equivalence, and gamma(a-bar)=Rv^*(gamma a)o gamma(eta_P) gives the exact adjoint-map criterion. Small cases checked: empty I, one object, a contractible simplicial monoid, empty mapping sets. The duplicate search with rg found only special or different statements (lem-coef-simplicial-presheaf-projective-model, lem-coef-combinatorial-presheaf-presentation) and no cycle. No new nodes, no fixes."
 },
